<title>GREECE: LATEST VOTE COUNT IN GREEK ELECTION.</title>
<headline>LATEST VOTE COUNT IN GREEK ELECTION.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Latest provisional results in</p>
<p>Greece's national elections won on Sunday by socialist Prime</p>
<p>Minister Costas Simitis, with 99.6 percent of votes counted,</p>
<p>according to Interior Ministry figures released on Monday:</p>
<p> Party		     percentage of vote	    Seats</p>
<p>PASOK (socialists)		41.51		162</p>
<p>New Democracy (conservatives)	38.13		108</p>
<p>KKE (Communist Party)		 5.6		 11</p>
<p> Coalition of the Left	     5.11		10</p>
<p> Democratic Social Movement	4.43		 9</p>
<p> Political Spring		    2.94		 -</p>
<p> Others				  2.28		 -</p>
<p>-- Final results will be available on Tuesday, when counts</p>
<p>from all remote polling stations come in. A party needs three</p>
<p>percent of the vote to enter parliament. Seats are provisional</p>
<p>pending the final count.</p>
</text>
